  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Janardhan Mandal & Anr vs State Of Jharkhand on 13 June, 2016 Author: Rongon Mukhopadhyay Bench: Rongon Mukhopadhyay In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr. M.P. No. 05 of 2011 ------ 1. Janardhan Mandal, S/o late Suresh Mandal 2. Murlidhar Mandal, S/o late Suresh Mandal Both are resident of Ghormara, P.O.-Ghormara Bazar, P.S.- Mohanpur, District- Deoghar ... ... Petitioners Versus The State of Jharkhand ... ... Opposite Party ------ Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rongon Mukhopadhyay ------ For the Petitioners : Mrs. Vandana Singh, Advocate Mr. Sudhansu Kumar Deo, Advocate",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Mrs. Vandana Singh, learned counsel appearing for the petitioners submits that the report of public analyst of the State was never served upon the petitioners and only on receiving notice by the Civil Surgeon, an application was made by the petitioners on 28.05.2008, for sending the sample to the Central Food Laboratory, Kolkata. Learned counsel for the petitioners further submits that non submission of the report of the public analyst means violation of Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, as the valuable right of the petitioners have been curbed.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mrs. Vandana Singh, learned counsel appearing for the petitioners submits that the report of public analyst of the State was never served upon the petitioners and only on receiving notice by the Civil Surgeon, an application was made by the petitioners on 28.05.2008, for sending the sample to the Central Food Laboratory, Kolkata. Learned counsel for the petitioners further submits that non submission of the report of the public analyst means violation of Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, as the valuable right of the petitioners have been curbed.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
